course: dictionary
lesson: 8981
title: Sis, the casual word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sis is a short, friendly word for sister. You will hear it in chatty speech and casual texts. «Hey sis, can I borrow your bike?» Here sis means your sister, and the relaxed tone shows you are close.
explain: Sis can also be a friendly name for a close female friend, not only a sister. Someone might call their best mate sis. The word shows warmth and closeness, not a family link. The clues are who is speaking and how they say it.
explain: Sis is informal slang, so keep it for casual talk and texts. Do not use it in formal writing, such as a school essay or a letter to the headteacher. Phrases like little sis and big sis show which sister is younger or older.
fact: Sis is an informal noun, short for sister.
fact: «Hey sis, can I borrow your bike?» uses sis when talking to your sister.
fact: Sis can also be a friendly name for a close female friend.
fact: Little sis and big sis are common phrases that show age order between sisters.
fact: In French, «sœurette» is cosy slang for little sis, just as «frérot» is slang for little bro.
exercise: «Hey sis, can I borrow your bike?» Who is sis most likely to be? | A road sign | A shop assistant | *Your sister | A teacher
exercise: Where should you NOT use the word sis? | A text to your sister | *A formal letter to the headteacher | A chat with a close friend | A note to your little sis
exercise: What does «little sis» tell you? | The sister is taller | The sister is ill | *The sister is the younger one | The sister is a teacher
test: Your friend calls her best mate «sis». What might she mean? | A girl she has never met | A cousin from Scotland | A school teacher | *A close female friend
test: Which French word is cosy slang for little sis? | frérot | bonjour | maman | *sœurette
exam: Why is sis fine in a text to your sister but not in a school essay? | Sis is a rude word | *It is informal slang, so it suits casual speech | It is only used for brothers | Sis means teacher in school
